The `permute` method first checks whether the current index is equal to the length of the input array. If it is, it adds the current permutation to the list of permutations and returns.

Otherwise, it finds the value at the current index and swaps it with the value at the next index. It then recursively calls the `permute` method with the updated array and the next index.

After the recursive call returns, the method swaps the values back to their original positions and continues to the next index.

